  "publicationRecovery": {
    "earlierBoundedRun": "Stopped before b009 database transaction because sustained reclaim stalled media upload; b000-b008 retained.",
    "fix": "Stream media request bodies, explicitly collect after validation and between optional CLI uploads; original resource limits preserved.",
    "deploymentRetry": "First fixed release rolled back when local disk exhaustion broke streamed logs. R2 uses server-local logs and completed successfully.",
    "resume": "Restarted at b009 using bounded chunks of at most three batches and at most 100 MiB referenced media; every batch retained health and stability gates.",
    "releaseLog": "build/original-production/deploy-r2.log",
    "audioTimeout": "At b036 two PUT attempts exceeded the prior 30-second short-clip request deadline. Published b035 retained. Changed only the audio PUT deadline to 90 seconds inside the existing 120-second signature and 600-second maintenance job; server memory/CPU/IO limits unchanged. Verified 43.2 MB HTTP upload with a 32-second response delay, then deployed the focused fix and resumed idempotently.",
    "finalReleaseLog": "build/original-production/deploy-8f84b5f0520b.log",
    "postUploadReclaim": "The extended upload completed, but the final media buffers remained before database allocation and caused sustained memory.high reclaim. Stopped that owned maintenance unit safely, retained assets and prior committed versions, and added an explicit CLI collection before creating the database connection. No memory/CPU/IO/runtime limits changed; unconfirmed batch resumed idempotently.",
    "fileStreaming": "Post-upload collection alone did not prevent in-flight whole-WAV buffers from exceeding memory.high. Changed original-file WAV validation and upload to bounded 64 KiB reads, preserving complete-file SHA, RIFF/PCM format, duration and peak checks, and cancelling/destroying upload streams after requests. Original file bytes and catalog hashes unchanged.",
    "receiptReconciliation": "A deliberately stopped systemd maintenance unit returned status zero without transaction receipts. Removed unconfirmed b036/b037 checkpoint entries and required matching CLI batch/hash/unit/response receipts before acknowledging any batch; final PostgreSQL verification independently confirms publication."
  }
